# V7 multi-request responsiveness, 2026-10-18

Machine: Ryzen 7 260, 16 GB RAM, RTX 5050 Laptop (8 GB, ~40 W). Model:
`~/models/Qwen3.5-4B-Q8`, `--backend cuda --quantize int8 --ctx 2048
--temp 0`, one release-build server per variant, warm model, nothing else on
the GPU. Load generator: `06-load.py PORT PID SCENARIO RUNS` (streaming
clients, TTFT = first non-empty SSE content delta, process RSS from
/proc, process VRAM and device util from nvidia-smi at 2 Hz).

Scenarios (client: arrival offset, prompt, max_tokens):
- solo_short: 1 x 47-token greeting, 32.
- solo_long: 1 x 1317-token code-review prompt, 64.
- three_interactive: 3 short prompts at +0/+0.05/+0.10 s, 32 each.
- long_plus_two: the 1317-token job at +0 s, short clients at +1 s and +2 s.

## Gates, fixed BEFORE implementation

Compared against the current sequential server (`BASE`) and, for
long_plus_two, against `BASE-WAIT`: the same binary with the 10 s queue wait
raised to 120 s so the interactive requests are not rejected (matched
conditions; the shipped limit is unchanged). Medians of three runs.

Correctness (all required):
- C1 Every client's greedy text is byte-identical to the same request run
  alone on BASE. Streamed text equals non-streamed text.
- C2 The engine and its HF-verified math are untouched. A real-model test
  must show prefill split into scheduler slices equals one-shot prefill:
  same greedy token, normalized max <= 1e-4, relative RMS <= 1e-5.
  The pinned Qwen3.5-4B Q8 CUDA `verify` figures must be unchanged.
- C3 Per-request KV/DeltaNet state is never shared. Concurrent sessions are
  isolated; a session in use by another request is refused, not mixed;
  checkpoint reuse still skips >= 90% of turn-one tokens; disconnect, 300 s
  cancel, inference failure and changed-prefix fallback leave the session
  and the next request intact.
- C4 Bounded admission: active requests <= a fixed cap derived from free VRAM;
  at most two more wait in FIFO order; further connections get 503; wait
  >10 s gives 408.

Latency / throughput (all required):
- L1 long_plus_two: both interactive requests succeed (BASE: 408) and their
  TTFT p95 <= 2.0 s (BASE-WAIT: ~11.4 s).
- L2 three_interactive: p95 TTFT at least 25% below BASE (1.87 s -> <= 1.40 s)
  and p50 TTFT within +10% of BASE (0.95 s).
- T1 Aggregate SSE events/s on three_interactive and long_plus_two >= 95% of
  BASE-WAIT; long_plus_two makespan <= BASE-WAIT +5%.
- T2 The long job in long_plus_two completes in <= 1.25x its solo BASE time
  (12.0 s -> <= 15.0 s).
- T3 No solo regression: solo_short TTFT and solo_long total time within +5%
  of BASE; decode events/s within -5%.

Memory (all required):
- M1 Three repeated long_plus_two runs: second-to-third process RSS and
  process VRAM growth each < 128 MiB; device free VRAM at peak >= 512 MiB.

Decision: keep the scheduler only if every gate passes. Otherwise revert it
and record NO-GO with the failing numbers. Continuous batching is added only
if, after interleaving, aggregate decode throughput is the measured limit.

